## 4. Working with properties

Properties are the primary resource in the Roomly API. Most integrations start here.

### 4.1 List properties

```http
GET /v1/properties
```

```bash
curl "https://api.roomly.com.ng/v1/properties" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $ROOMLY_API_KEY"
```

Without filters, this returns the first page of all properties. Full response shape and pagination fields are covered in [8.1](#81-pagination).

### 4.2 Filter properties

Filters combine as `AND` conditions. The full parameter list — `school`, `area`, `minPrice`, `maxPrice`, `propertyType`, `gender`, `verified`, `available` — is in the [API Specification](/blog/roomly-api-specification#list-properties). In practice, most real searches stack three or four at once:

```bash
curl "https://api.roomly.com.ng/v1/properties?school=school_futminna&propertyType=self_contain&minPrice=150000&maxPrice=300000&verified=true&available=true" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $ROOMLY_API_KEY"
```

An unmatched combination of filters returns an empty `data` array, not an error. Build your UI for that explicitly — an empty state, not a failure message.

### 4.3 Retrieve a property

```http
GET /v1/properties/{propertyId}
```

```bash
curl "https://api.roomly.com.ng/v1/properties/prop_123" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $ROOMLY_API_KEY"
```

This returns fields the list endpoint omits — `description` and `amenities` — which is why a detail page should always call this endpoint directly rather than reusing data from a list response. See [7.2](#72-build-a-property-details-page).

### 4.4 Check availability

```http
GET /v1/properties/{propertyId}/availability
```

```bash
curl "https://api.roomly.com.ng/v1/properties/prop_123/availability" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $ROOMLY_API_KEY"
```

This is served separately from the property record because it changes far more often than the rest of a listing. Treat it as near-real-time: don't cache it, and re-check it immediately before a booking action rather than trusting an earlier response. See [9.3](#93-caching-and-stale-data).

